{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1152367-selecting-rotes-2e","id":1152367,"title":"Selecting Rotes [2E]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-23T19:25:06-07:00","id":1152367,"title":"Selecting Rotes [2E]","content":"New Mage player here, and I just wanted to confirm something that I think I understand correctly, but I'm not confident. When players are selecting Rotes for their characters, do you simply look at the sample spells listed, and at the Suggest Rote Skills for that spell, and if one or more of those align with your Order's preferred Rote Skills, then you can just say, &quot;That's the Rote skill I'm going to use!&quot; and call it good? Is it that simple? Is it allowable to pick a different Order skill than one that is listed on the spell, or even one completely different from the 3 suggested, or your 3 Order skills? (I suspect the answer to that last question is no, but I'm trying to understand things.)<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> Path - Obrimos<br /> Order - Mysterium<br /> Order Rote Skills - Investigation, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> Spell - As Above, So Below (Prime oo)<br /> Suggested Rote Skills - Academics, Occult, Politics<br /> <br /> So if a Mysterium mage is taking this spell as a Rote, would Occult be my only option for the skill? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19654-razorstorm","name":"Razorstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T19:29:55-07:00","id":1152370,"title":"","content":"No, the encoded skill of a Rote can be any skill, and you may have been taught a non-Mysterium member during the phase when Orders were trying to recruit you before the Mysterium won you over, or by a mentor or grimoire with an eclectic selection of rotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T22:44:09-07:00","id":1152412,"title":"","content":"Some of my characters deliberately have rotes that are just useless or niche use because they seem like things someone would want if they didn't know they were going to be having an extraordinary life from now on--My go-to character usually has Tune-In because she wants free radio whenever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T23:10:22-07:00","id":1152413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1152367-selecting-rotes-2e?p=1152370#post1152370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the encoded skill of a Rote can be any skill, and you may have been taught a non-Mysterium member during the phase when Orders were trying to recruit you before the Mysterium won you over, or by a mentor or grimoire with an eclectic selection of rotes.</div> </div> </div> </div>What he said. I definitely prioritize flavor and story richness or min-max optimizations, unless you can do that well too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T04:20:31-07:00","id":1152458,"title":"","content":"Okay, so basically it's &quot;pick a few spells you want to be very competent with, and pick a skill that makes some sorta sense to go with it, which may or may not be one of your Order's preferred skills?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19654-razorstorm","name":"Razorstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T04:50:05-07:00","id":1152465,"title":"","content":"Pretty much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T10:01:20-07:00","id":1152542,"title":"","content":"Of course, nothing stops you from having all your Rotes use Order Rote Skills, it's just not really not worth trying to milk that bonus for every Rote compared to having the Rote in the first place.<br /> <br /> It's also worth thinking a bit about Praxis spells vs. Rote spells when picking your starting ones. The Praxis spell bonus is better for spells you use a lot, but generally aren't going to bother with a bunch of spell factors or Reach, whereas the Rote spell bonus for learning the rote (instead of using one from a grimoire) are better for spells that get more complicated when used (ex: pretty much anything you want for regular casting in combat or similarly paced scenes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}